**  
The bug exists because Go’s `net/http.FileServer` applies `filepath.Clean` after dot-removal, allowing `../../../../../../etc/passwd` to resolve to `/var/www/static/../../../../../../etc/passwd` → `/etc/passwd`. The exploit sends:
```
GET /static/ HTTP/1.1
Accept-Language: ../../../../../etc/passwd
```
The server returns the file contents. To sanitise in Nginx:
```nginx
location ~* \.(go|goc|gohtml)$ {
    set $valid_accept_language "";
    if ($http_accept_language !~* ^[a-z]{2,3}(?:-[a-z]{2,3})?(?:;q=[0-9]\.[0-9])?(?:, ?[a-z]{2,3}(?:-[a-z]{2,3})?(?:;q=[0-9]\.[0-9])?)*$) {
        set $valid_accept_language "D";
    }
    if ($valid_accept_language = "") {
        return 403;
    }
}
```
Mitigation: upgrade Go ≥1.22.2, use `http.StripPrefix("/static/", http.FileServer(fs))`. Real-world: Google VRP 2024 rewarded $20k for this bypass of `FileServer`.

